{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"undyed-unheedful-conure","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nThe live `completion-verifier` standing eval constructs one PydanticAIRunner before entering its per-case disposable repositories. `eval_solver.run_case` correctly passes a per-case `repo_root`, but the explicit runner override retains its original `LLMConfig.repo_path`. `runner._effective_config` substitutes only the request model, so filesystem and ticket tools read the checkout instead of each case fixture.\n\n## Evidence\nA full live run had coverage 1.0 but epoch_pass `[False, False, False]`. Targeted complete cases searched `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-debug-completion-9895` and cited `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/completion-verifier.eval.yaml`; they did not see fixture files such as `src/cli.py` or `app/profile.py`. Operator-attested cases, which need no fixture code, passed. Code path: `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval.py::_live_solver` builds one runner; `src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py::run_case` creates the disposable repo; `src/rebar/llm/runner.py::_effective_config` preserves the runner base `repo_path`.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a RED eval-solver contract proving an explicitly injected reusable live-style runner reads each disposable case root.\n- Re-root the effective per-request config without weakening the run-wide budget/config floor or model override semantics.\n- Validate completion, ticket-quality, and spec-alignment disposable-store cases plus ordinary workflow runner reuse.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A deterministic test reproduces a completion eval reading the wrong checkout root before the fix.\n- [ ] Every agentic eval case reads its own disposable fixture repository and ticket store.\n- [ ] Existing per-step model substitution and run-wide floor semantics remain unchanged.\n- [ ] The full live `completion-verifier` standing eval passes its declared `at_least(2)` gate with coverage at least 0.8.","id":"ca47-e124-7462-44d0","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Standing completion eval reads the checkout instead of disposable fixture repos"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786274115987289001,"uuid":"78ea6d59-3fd0-4171-a5d6-a8c6cbd58e45"}